	(text "Auto TX enable, all logic on 3.3 V.\nTX low -> D1 discharges RC -> TXEN high: U3 drives the bus, U4 output off.\nTX high -> R1*C6 (6.8 us) recharges RC; TXEN stays high 3.3-7.3 us after the last\n  low, so the driver is held through the packet and only the first edge is delayed\n  (target <= 20 ns). The servo starts replying ~21 us after the packet.\nC6: C0G. D1: low-leakage small-signal Schottky. C1 / C4 / C5 decouple U1 / U3 / U4.\nR4 bleeds current pushed into +3.3V if the servo pulls the bus up to 5 V.\nTP1 (TXEN) is a probe point for the AtomS3R bench (3.3 V logic).\nDesign notes: digital_servo/atoms3r/docs/ttl_board_redesign.md"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 170.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2a814d8a-a516-5ce2-92e6-92e488fde3e4")
	)
